{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455730-gain-generation-with-new-mechanincs","id":1455730,"title":"Gain generation with new mechanincs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-28T14:32:09-07:00","id":1455730,"title":"Gain generation with new mechanincs","content":"With my friends we plan to play vampires that stay as humans as possible, increasing our humanity and even, why not, reach golconda. The purpose of our story is to protect humans to survive with them when the gehenna will come and the first vampires will return.<br /> To survive until then we need to get stronger, but the only way to do so is the amaranth, which would get us in trouble with the anciant powerfull vampire that rules over the world and control cities.<br /> <br /> I've thout about Cain, from the &quot;Book of Nod&quot; the vampirism is a gift of Lillith, plus the weakness which are due to the archangels. But thanks to &quot;Werewolf the apocalypse&quot; we know the other side of the world: the Umbra, the spirits, the triat...<br /> From those informations we could imagine the real story of cain: granted immortality by a powerfull spirit and cursed by a banes who felt the potential of a great plague. The immortality gift plus the bane curse could have created Vampirism (if some of you have better origin story i would be happy to know them, i love the character and would love to learn a non bible legend)<br /> <br /> From that point we know that to gain generation a vampire have to do the Amaranth on a lower generation vampire to steal his power. But if the origin of vampirism is spiritual, we could imagine a new way to lower our generation, vampires have already faced spirits and these spirits can materialize in the physical world.<br /> So if a vampire feed on a spirit to steel his strength et feed the very essence of the vampirism curse that afflict him, he could possibly get stronger and lower his generation without doing the amaranth, after all you don't meet a spirit everyday and they are not so easy to defeat with their powers, and they cannot travel between world just like that, especially in cities.<br /> <br /> Of course we can adapt that new rule by selecting a specific spirit that would feed vampirism essnce, a blood spirit obviously but maybe others.<br /> That way we could complete the world of darkness with more bonds between the games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T21:10:38-07:00","id":1455742,"title":"","content":"Strictly speaking, each Storyteller can allow whatever they like at their table. But the vast majority of Cainites have an extremely hard time interacting with the spiritual world of the wider WoD. It's also a question of how much feeding/stealing that you're talking about; if you're talking about the vampire consuming the spirit in it's entirety, that sounds like it has a fair bit in common with Diablerie, and you have to potentially settle some questions about whether or not consuming a spirit in that fashion might still produce Diablerie marks in the aura. It's also the kind of behaviour that could put ashing a Kindred at the top of the local Garou's list of priorities. If you're not talking about completely consuming a spirit in the process, then it has a lot of potential to become very broken if more than a rare handful of spirits can produce that effect. Alternatively, it's the sort of thing that should require the development of a Discipline or some kind of Blood Magic.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that the angle you're approaching this from kind of seems to try and avoid one of the central conflicts of the game, the struggle to retain Humanity when doing what you need in order to survive often threatens it. And while only a small handful of vampires interact with the Umbra, there are those who have been at it for millennia, and you'd have to question why such a powerful tool wouldn't be more prevalent if it was readily available to them.<br /> <br /> Regarding the idea that the Umbra is the source of vampirism, not the Abrahamic God, the Garou have their own story of the First Vampire, &quot;the Bloody Man,&quot; which could be a foundation to build on if you go ahead with your idea. Depending on the version of the game you're playing, other options for lowering Generation, temporarily or permanently, exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T02:37:50-07:00","id":1455747,"title":"","content":"Well i was thinking about consumming an entire spirit, but if i go with that idea of vampirism that would be a corrupted gift from a bane, then the only way to lower the generation would be to consume a bane, the wyrm corruption could be the key to increase the vampirism essence.<br /> &quot;The bloody man&quot;, as we played the v20 of werewolf the apocalypse i may have missed that story, i'll check it soon.<br /> Concerning the humanity, well directly feed the beast inside with spiritual essence would have even more effect than the &quot;simple&quot; Diablerie. Of course it will leave marks on the aura but not with the usual ones, and will make other vampire curious and attract the adepts of Amaranth. In addition the humanity loss would be bigger, the beast instinct getting so powerful that it would litteraly consume the mind of the vampire and eventually leaving marks on the body (impossibility to retract fangs, bloody red eyes, increased hunger, more frequent frenzy ...) <br /> It is said that vampires that reach golconda are respected by werewolves (not allies or friends but at least respected beings), so hunting banes would be an interesting way to play and the only way to lower generation would be to feed and consume completely a bane (it wouldn't work with fomori cause they're possessed, the banes would die or fly with the host being killed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T08:54:42-07:00","id":1455755,"title":"","content":"Consuming Banes would probably clash with any effort to pursue Golconda, as you'd be regularly consuming the tainted essence of Wyrm spirits. It would also probably run the risk of having the vampire in question register as even more Wyrm-tainted than usual to the Garou. But if you lean into the idea that Vampirism really is of the Wyrm, it's not completely unreasonable. Although I would still strongly recommend requiring some kind of special power or technique, not just let a vampire sink their fangs into a Bane and diablerize it.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that &quot;werewolves get along with vampires in Golconda&quot; is a bit of a mixed bag. I think there's a non-English source that supports the idea, but I've never heard it come up else where. Of course, vampires with high Humanity (8+ IIRC) do not register as Wyrm-tainted to the Garou, but that's as likely to be seen as some kind of trickery as anything. I don't think most Garou are familiar with the idea of Golconda, with a lot of RIPANDTEAR first, ask questions never. But exceptions exist.<br /> <br /> Regarding other methods of lowering Generation, especially if you're playing the X20 lines: the Banu Haqim possess a ritual that allows them to lower Generation without diablerie by collecting tons of vitae and turning it into an alchemical mixture. Tremere Thaumaturgy has the Path of Blood, which allows one to temporarily lower Generation at the final level. There's also a ritual that allows multiple vampires to benefit from a single diablerie, but I can't recall the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T15:36:20-07:00","id":1455767,"title":"","content":"I've learn about the &quot;Bloody man&quot; legend on the white wolf wiki, i would like to know the entire story but the weaver and the non corrupted wyrm being the creators of vampirism is exactly what i was thinking and explain why the low generations vampire are so powerfull, their strength come from 2 of the triat.<br /> <br /> The garou hates vampire so we was not planning to get friends or negociate with them, as the gm prefer garou to vampire he will be sadistic with the players x)<br /> <br /> An alchemical mixture created from a lot of vitae is a great way too, if you remember the source so i can go and find out more details about it.<br /> <br /> From the v5 of vampire the mascarade there is some blood rituals to be safe when spirits are around, we could imagine a new ritual to trap banes or an elixir to be able to interact with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T21:25:08-07:00","id":1455782,"title":"","content":"The ritual is called &quot;From Marduk's Throat.&quot; I don't know a specific source, but you can find it on the wiki probably. It's a major league secret of a clan of vampire assassins, so trying to get your hands on it would be a pretty epic (and likely fatal) adventure.<br /> <br /> Most wiki pages include sources where you can find out where the details of stories like the Bloody Man are recorded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T09:18:22-07:00","id":1455800,"title":"","content":"From Marduk's Throat is in Lore of the Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T12:14:09-07:00","id":1455808,"title":"","content":"As far as spirits go, vampires mostly act like insect traps. Most spirits avoid them, some foolishly try to possess vampires before being overcome by the curse of caine without the vampire even noticing. Only a few provide tangible results from a merger, but those possession results are messy. <br /> <br /> Find some consenting suicidalists and then start enfolding the believers (rites of the blood) or arrange a deal with a demon. If you use V1/V2 diablerie rules (the superior rules) you can diablerize without automatic humanity loss (It's normal murder) so if you eat a deserving, heinous criminal, there are mitigating factors to your humanity roll. Bardo is a good cheat.<br /> <br /> Honestly I don't think you're being very realistic. You don't really need Diablerie to gain strength (unless we're talking V5 in which the best method to gain disciplines bar perhaps resonance farming is to devour the young.) Going wide with Disciplines/Developing attributes/making up for your inadequacies with equipment/resources are all good strategies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-30-2021, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T16:27:02-07:00","id":1455823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455730-gain-generation-with-new-mechanincs?p=1455808#post1455808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as spirits go, vampires mostly act like insect traps. Most spirits avoid them, some foolishly try to possess vampires before being overcome by the curse of caine without the vampire even noticing. Only a few provide tangible results from a merger, but those possession results are messy.<br /> <br /> Find some consenting suicidalists and then start enfolding the believers (rites of the blood) or arrange a deal with a demon. If you use V1/V2 diablerie rules (the superior rules) you can diablerize without automatic humanity loss (It's normal murder) so if you eat a deserving, heinous criminal, there are mitigating factors to your humanity roll. Bardo is a good cheat.<br /> <br /> Honestly I don't think you're being very realistic. You don't really need Diablerie to gain strength (unless we're talking V5 in which the best method to gain disciplines bar perhaps resonance farming is to devour the young.) Going wide with Disciplines/Developing attributes/making up for your inadequacies with equipment/resources are all good strategies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot that ritual in RotB, good suggestion.<br /> <br /> It's also worth pointing out that while the specific details of what you get for attaining Golconda are mostly not put into rules, there is at least strong evidence that one of the benefits is surpassing the limits of Generation on your ability to learn Disciplines above 5 dots. I don't recall for sure how it might relate to other benefits of Generation like size of Blood Pool or resistance to Dominate. But pursuing Golconda and climbing the Generation ladder tend to be somewhat mutually exclusive pursuits; you're likely to handicap your attempt at one if you chase the other.<br /> <br /> Also, don't ignore less obvious or direct forms of power; your characters may not pack the punch of elder vampires, but information and allies can help tip the balance in your favour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T16:52:35-07:00","id":1455884,"title":"","content":"How many way are there to lower the generation permanently? As i only have the v20, v5 and the black hand book i don't know if there's more in previous edition or other books","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T21:32:47-07:00","id":1455900,"title":"","content":"Apologies for being repetitive, but to some extent, it's a &quot;depends on the table&quot; question. Even from the canonically listed options, there are probably options that a Storyteller could choose to leave out if it just didn't fit the themes of their story.<br /> <br /> Aside from Diablerie, the rituals listed above are the only options available in canon AFAIK. Something I suspect canon may support, and that I would probably approve, is that lowering Generation might be possible through pacts with powerful spirits or demons. But not run-of-the-mill spirits and demons. It's the sort of thing a demigod or demon prince might be able to provide, but not your average Jaggling.<br /> <br /> Again, lowering Generation is supposed to be very hard, if not impossible, if you aren't willing to murderrapecannibalize the soul of another more powerful vampire in the process. It's supposed to be a component of how Kindred society is stratified between elder vampires and their juniors. Generation wouldn't be precious if it was just a Trait that anyone could increase by grinding. Depending on who you ask, the power struggle over Generation is one of the most defining aspects of vampire society in VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T21:30:43-07:00","id":1457176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455730-gain-generation-with-new-mechanincs?p=1455884#post1455884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many way are there to lower the generation permanently? As i only have the v20, v5 and the black hand book i don't know if there's more in previous edition or other books</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, we don't know your ST's position on the matter, and it makes all the difference. Like, all of it. Is it only the players planning this? Is your ST open to rules suggestions? Or are you planning on trying to sell your thoughts as The Logical Canon? Or yet, is your ST on board already and asking for ideas? This all makes for very different situations.<br /> <br /> As default, the only canon ways to permanently change Generation are Diablerie and the Assamite ritual. And this last ritual is what it is, good luck getting your hands on it and then better luck using it all the way up. The canon do not outright forbid other methods existing, but do not assumes them either.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but as pointed before you're probably putting a lot of weight on the wrong place. By itself, lowering generation only gets you more blood and blood per round. Even attaining higher levels of Disciplines is easier said than done, and maybe not all that interesting. Seriously, a lot of those powers are pretty lame for the hideously high cost in XP. Get other disciplines instead. Certainly pumping more blood is a great advantage, but a 3rd gen neonate isn't really all that more powerful if it have only a beginner's sheet.<br /> <br /> By the way, blood still needs to come from somewhere. Pumping more blood means needing more blood. How do you pretend to manage your sources? Most of the time a 8th gen consumption rate is more than you really want to use, even if you're a Blood God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}